      "trap_id": "SAS-12",
      "description": "One policy per row, each with written_eur exactly on or just beside a band edge: -10.00 and -0.01 (NEGATIVE), 0.00 (lower bound of 0-249, included), 249.99 and 250.00 (either side of the 250 edge), 499.99 and 500.00, 999.99, 1000.00 (included in 1000+) and 1000.01. A naive CASE WHEN that uses <= instead of < on the upper bounds, or > 1000 for the top band, puts 0, 250, 500 or 1000 in the wrong band. written_eur is NOT NULL here, so the NULL-to-UNKNOWN branch can't be reached with legal inputs.",
